{
  "id": "L-006",
  "title": "The Intermediate Value Theorem",
  "atom_ids": ["A-06"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Continuity on an interval means continuity at every point of the interval, with one-sided continuity at the endpoints: continuous on "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "[a, b]" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means continuous at every "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "(a, b)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", right-continuous at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and left-continuous at "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "b" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". With that in hand, continuity has a striking consequence — the intermediate value theorem."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": "Intermediate value theorem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is continuous on "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "[a, b]" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "N" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is any number between "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(a)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(b)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", then there exists a "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "c" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " in "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "(a, b)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(c) = N" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". In words: a continuous function on an interval takes every value between its endpoint values."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "src": "figures/ivt.png",
      "atom_id": "A-06",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The function "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(x) = x^3 - x - 1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is continuous on "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "[1, 2]" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", where "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(1) = -1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(2) = 5" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Since 0 lies between them, the theorem guarantees a "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "c" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(c) = 0" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — here "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "c \\approx 1.325" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the dark point where the curve crosses the axis."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "A root exists, without finding it",
      "problem": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Show that "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(x) = x^3 - x - 1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " has a root in "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "[1, 2]" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — an "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(x) = 0" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — without solving the equation."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The function is a polynomial, hence continuous everywhere, in particular on "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "[1, 2]" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The endpoints are "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "f(1) = 1 - 1 - 1 = -1" },
          { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
          { "type": "math", "source": "f(2) = 8 - 2 - 1 = 5" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The number 0 lies between "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "-1" },
          { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
          { "type": "math", "source": "5" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", so the intermediate value theorem applies with "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "N = 0" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Conclusion: there exists "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "c" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "(1, 2)" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "f(c) = 0" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The theorem does not say where "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "c" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is — only that it exists."
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "widget",
      "name": "plot",
      "version": "1.0",
      "parameters": {
        "series": [
          {
            "label": "f(x) = x^3 - x - 1",
            "points": [
              [1.0, -1.0], [1.1, -0.769], [1.2, -0.472], [1.3, -0.103],
              [1.35, 0.11], [1.4, 0.344], [1.5, 0.875], [1.6, 1.496],
              [1.7, 2.213], [1.8, 3.032], [1.9, 3.959], [2.0, 5.0]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "xlabel": "x",
        "ylabel": "y",
        "title": "x^3 - x - 1 crosses zero between x = 1 and x = 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "important",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The intermediate value theorem is an existence statement, not a recipe. It proves that a root lies in the interval; finding it — by bisection, a graphing tool, or a better guess — is a separate job. And the endpoint values must straddle "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "N" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": if both are above "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "N" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the theorem says nothing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "formative",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The function "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x}" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " has "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g(-1) = -1" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g(1) = 1" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". A friend applies the intermediate value theorem to conclude that "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "g" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " has a zero in "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "[-1, 1]" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Explain precisely why the theorem cannot be used here."
        }
      ],
      "kind": "free_response"
    }
  ]
}
